SQL Server Plan Viewer for DBX
==============================

An independent, offline viewer for SQL Server ShowPlan XML. It adds View Plan
beside the DBX result grid and a standalone workbench for paste and local files.
No SQL is executed. No database permission, AI service, native sidecar, runtime
network request, or DBX host modification is needed.

Usage
-----
1. Open a result containing complete SQL Server ShowPlan XML and choose View Plan.
2. Choose the plan cell, then the statement. All supplied matching cells and
   statements remain selectable, including statements without an operator tree.
3. Select an operator for XML-derived properties. Use the zoom buttons, Fit,
   and background dragging to navigate. Source XML shows the original document.
4. Alternatively open the standalone workbench, then Paste XML or Open file
   (.sqlplan or .xml).

Cost is estimated subtree cost, not measured elapsed time or a percentage.
Actual rows are shown only when runtime counters exist. Object/index details
and predicates come from the supplied XML; missing properties are not inferred.
DBX passes at most 500 result rows. The viewer reports truncated result context;
use the original file or paste the full value for omitted/truncated data.
Limits: 10 MiB per XML document, 5,000 operators, 150,000 XML elements.
DTD/entity declarations are rejected. Files are processed in memory, not saved.

Installation
------------
Build or download the .dbxp package, then open DBX Plugin Center and install the
local package. An unsigned development package requires Allow unsigned
development packages. Enable that setting only if you choose to trust this
source/build. The plugin requests no host permissions.

A GitHub unsigned release is separate from a signed Marketplace listing.
Marketplace review and signing are controlled by DBX Store maintainers.
This initial implementation is undergoing verification; a published source tree
alone does not establish successful desktop installation or Store acceptance.

Development
-----------
Requires Node.js/npm and the pinned development dependencies in package-lock.json.

  npm ci
  npx playwright install chromium
  npm test
  npm run build
  npm run test:browser
  npm run package

The package includes only manifest.json, assets, and the generated self-contained
ui/index.html. Test fixtures are synthetic. Never commit live execution plans,
query results, credentials, or local environment files.

